    * statement: UPDATE brand_memory_items SET text=$1::VARCHAR, metadata=$2::JSON WHERE brand_memory_items.id = $3::VARCHAR
    * parameters: ('- Brand Identity & Naming Strategy: Exploring four primary naming directions (European/Latin roots like Aura Soy/Vela & Co., Direct/Descriptive like The Soy Wick/Pure Pours, Sensory & Wellness like Hygge Home/Soothe & Glow, and Artisanal/Cozy like Dafaye/Nour) to establish an emotional connection and minimalist aesthetic.\n- Pricing Strategy: \n  - Standard/Medium Jar (180-200g): EGP 382 to 450 (Targeting the Mid-Range sweet spot with a healthy 2.5x to 3x COGS markup).\n  - Large/Double-Wick Jar (300-350g): EGP 600 to 680 (Positioned as a smart, eco-friendly local alternative to imported luxury brands like Bath & Body Works).\n  - Mini Jar/Travel Tin (100g): EGP 200 to 250 (Serving as an entry point for customer acquisition, discovery sets, and giveaways).\n- Advertising & Launch Campaign Strategy:\n  - Budget Allocation: Balanced Growth Package recommended with a total launch budget of EGP 12,000 to 15,000 (approx. 35% allocated to a 2-week Teaser phase for waitlist/leads and 65% to a 2-3 week Launch/Conversion phase).\n  - Campaign Phases: \n    1. Teaser Phase (Behind-the-scenes, soy wax pouring, aesthetic mood lighting, focus on clean-burning health benefits).\n    2. Launch Phase (Carousel and Video Reels highlighting upcycled glass vessels, multi-cycle home decor utility, and strong scent throw).\n    3. Retargeting (Social proof, reviews, and comparative value messaging against expensive imported alternatives).\n  - Geographic & Demographic Targeting: Urban centers (Cairo, Giza, Alexandria) focusing on demographics aged 24-45 with interests in home decor, interior design, wellness, self-care, and premium fragrance brands.', {'active_plans': '- Brand Identity & Naming Strategy: Exploring four primary naming directions (European/Latin roots like Aura Soy/Vela & Co., Direct/Descriptive like The Soy Wick/Pure Pours, Sensory & Wellness like Hygge Home/Soothe & Glow, and Artisanal/Cozy like Dafaye/Nour) to establish an emotional connection and minimalist aesthetic.\n- Pricing Strategy: \n  - Standard/Medium Jar (180-200g): EGP 382 to 450 (Targeting the Mid-Range sweet spot with a healthy 2.5x to 3x COGS markup).\n  - Large/Double-Wick Jar (300-350g): EGP 600 to 680 (Positioned as a smart, eco-friendly local alternative to imported luxury brands like Bath & Body Works).\n  - Mini Jar/Travel Tin (100g): EGP 200 to 250 (Serving as an entry point for customer acquisition, discovery sets, and giveaways).\n- Advertising & Launch Campaign Strategy:\n  - Budget Allocation: Balanced Growth Package recommended with a total launch budget of EGP 12,000 to 15,000 (approx. 35% allocated to a 2-week Teaser phase for waitlist/leads and 65% to a 2-3 week Launch/Conversion phase).\n  - Campaign Phases: \n    1. Teaser Phase (Behind-the-scenes, soy wax pouring, aesthetic mood lighting, focus on clean-burning health benefits).\n    2. Launch Phase (Carousel and Video Reels highlighting upcycled glass vessels, multi-cycle home decor utility, and strong scent throw).\n    3. Retargeting (Social proof, reviews, and comparative value messaging against expensive imported alternatives).\n  - Geographic & Demographic Targeting: Urban centers (Cairo, Giza, Alexandria) focusing on demographics aged 24-45 with interests in home decor, interior design, wellness, self-care, and premium fragrance brands.', 'source': 'ltm_compressor', 'created_at': '2026-10-11T20:11:09.435131+00:00', 'updated_at': '2026-10-12T10:24:48.051666+00:00'}, 'mem_plan_ba3c879d057b')
